        <item>
            <title>0.2.7</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 20 Mar 2026 18:21:17 -0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1774055866</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.2.7</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
  body { font-family: -apple-system, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; padding: 12px; }
  h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 14px; }
  h2 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 12px; }
  ul { margin: 4px 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  li { margin: 2px 0; }
</style>
<h3>What's New</h3>
<h2>New Features</h2>
<ul>
<li>Context compression recovery — When Claude Code compresses your conversation context mid-session, Addy now detects it automatically, shows a system message explaining what happened, and sends a recovery prompt summarizing your recent conversation so the agent can pick up where it left off. A second compression suggests starting a fresh conversation.</li>
<li>Context usage gauge — A new progress bar in the chat footer shows how much of Claude's context window you've used (e.g. "42k/200k"), turning yellow at 65% and orange at 85% so you know when compression is approaching.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Improvements</h2>
<ul>
<li>Attachment previews in sent messages — Images and files you attach to a chat message now appear as inline chips in the message bubble after sending, so you can see what was included in each turn.</li>
<li>Richer attachment previews in the composer — Pasted images now show an actual thumbnail preview instead of a generic file icon, and file attachments display a themed document icon with the file extension label.</li>
<li>Hover-to-reveal remove button on attachment chips — The remove button on file attachment chips in the composer is now hidden by default and smoothly fades in on hover, reducing visual clutter.</li>
</ul>

The release notes are saved to `/tmp/addy-release-notes.html`.
]]></description>
